late without that slot composes unchanged. A sitting composed from several judgement kinds carries the questions once. An absent roster yields its no-perspective line, while an unreadable existing roster refuses composition and names the roster.\"\n+detail = \"A sitting brief for a decomposition round carries every declared perspective question applicable to that round and asks the verdict to name one outcome for each perspective. A decomposition round judges a system requirement awaiting first approval or an approved stakeholder need whose text is amended; another judged set carries no perspective question. The applicable set combines each amended need with each need named by a system requirement the sitting judges, including an amended system requirement, widens each need by the authoring work item's declared tags, and evaluates each need alone. Questions fill the perspective slot only when the sitting template declares it; a template without that slot composes unchanged. A sitting composed from several judgement kinds carries the questions once. An absent roster yields its no-perspective line, while an unreadable existing roster refuses composition and names the roster.\"\n rationale = \"A decomposition review needs the applicable questions in the same brief and verdict that record its judgement. Treating each parent need independently prevents tags from one sibling widening another, while an optional slot preserves briefs that do not conduct a decomposition review.\"\n test_refs = \"TC-399\"\n status = \"Drafted\"\ndiff --git a/docs/requirements/system-requirements.toml b/docs/requirements/system-requirements.toml\nindex c1cc63f60..17b526377 100644\n--- a/docs/requirements/system-requirements.toml\n+++ b/docs/requirements/system-requirements.toml\n@@ -809,7 +809,7 @@ sn_refs = [\"SN-036\"]\n boundary_refs = [\"B-05\"]\n hat_refs = [\"TEST-ENGINEER\"]\n requirement = \"\"\"When a decomposition round is reviewed, the delivered planning content shall provide every applicable declared perspective's question in the decomposition brief and require the sitting's review record to name the outcome for each perspective.\"\"\"\n-rationale = \"\"\"A decomposition produced from one perspective can look complete while omitting security, operations or first-use failures. The hats roster and plan briefs already supply the applicable questions, and the sitting's review record preserves their outcomes; a separate machine-readable coverage record and checker would duplicate that review without improving its adequacy judgment. Hat-Refs remain the row-level provenance for perspectives that raised a requirement. This applies the owner ruling of 2026-09-06, re-affirmed 2026-10-13.\"\"\"\n+rationale = \"\"\"A decomposition produced from one perspective can look complete while omitting security, operations or first-use failures. The hats roster and the planning briefs already supply the applicable questions, and the sitting's review record preserves their outcomes; a separate machine-readable coverage record and checker would duplicate that review without improving its adequacy judgment. Hat-Refs remain the row-level provenance for perspectives that raised a requirement. This applies the owner ruling of 2026-09-06, re-affirmed 2026-10-13.\"\"\"\n acceptance_criteria = \"\"\"For one completed decomposition round, the applicable perspectives resolve from the declared hats roster, the decomposition brief presents each applicable perspective's question, and the sitting's review record names an outcome for every one; the independent adequacy review reads that record.\"\"\"\n priority = \"S\"\n verification = \"Inspection\"\n@@ -865,7 +865,7 @@ sn_refs = [\"SN-040\"]\n boundary_refs = [\"B-05\"]\n hat_refs = [\"MAINTAINER\"]\n requirement = \"The delivered planning content shall leave, with every component partition it produces, a machine-readable derivation record in the tracked component registry rather than session prose — the candidate partitions considered, the declared objective and constraints they were scored against, each candidate's score, the selected partition, and the human ruling that named the components and adopted it — such that a live component row whose record omits any of those elements, or a selection the recorded scores do not rank first without a recorded human override, is a reportable finding.\"\n-rationale = \"Realizes SN-040 — a free-form partition leaves no record of the alternatives weighed, so the next reviser cannot tell load-bearing boundaries from accidents; the record is what lets the choice be re-examined. SN-040 had no citing SR, even as the P5 partition work performed exactly this record. Reproducibility is stated as a recomputation from the record's own declared inputs, not as a reviewer re-running a model session, because only the former can fail — the SR-161 form applied to the partition instead of the perspective set. B-05 alone: the human ruling is an element the record must carry, not an observable the system states at the authority input, which is SR-139's and SR-140's ground.\"\n+rationale = \"Realizes SN-040 — a free-form partition leaves no record of the alternatives weighed, so the next reviser cannot tell load-bearing boundaries from accidents; the record is what lets the choice be re-examined. SN-040 had no citing SR, even as the P5 partition work performed exactly this record. Reproducibility is stated as a recomputation from the record's own declared inputs, not as a reviewer re-running a model session, because only the former can fail. B-05 alone: the human ruling is an element the record must carry, not an observable the system states at the authority input, which is SR-139's and SR-140's ground.\"\n acceptance_criteria = \"A partition round writes the derivation record into the tracked component registry, never into session prose or a plan document alone; a live component row with no record, or a record omitting the candidate partitions, the declared objective, the constraints, any candidate's score, the selected partition or the human ruling, is reported naming the missing element; a selected partition the recorded scores do not rank first is reported unless the record carries the human override that chose it; the recorded ranking recomputes from the record's own objective, constraints and scores alone.\"\n priority = \"S\"\n verification = \"Test\"\ndiff --git a/docs/test/test-cases.toml b/docs/test/test-cases.toml\nindex 7a3f9fa7a..87b937b78 100644\n--- a/docs/test/test-cases.toml\n+++ b/docs/test/test-cases.toml\n@@ -2181,7 +2181,7 @@ automated = \"No\"\n evidence = \"docs/test/inspection-procedures.md#decomposition-proportionality-inspection-result\"\n status = \"Approved\"\n phase = 5\n-inputs = [\"docs/test/inspection-procedures.md\", \"SR-161\", \"SR-186\", \"docs/requirements/hats.toml\"]\n+inputs = [\"docs/test/inspection-procedures.md\", \"SR-161\", \"SR-186\", \"docs/requirements/hats.toml\", \"docs/reviews/wi-976/011-ADJUDICATE-a46aad8.brief.md\", \"docs/reviews/wi-976/011-ADJUDICATE-a46aad8.md\"]\n max_age = 90\n rubric = \"docs/rubrics/decomposition-proportionality.md\"\n trigger = \"release\"\n@@ -3947,7 +3947,7 @@ phase = 6\n [test.TC-399]\n verifies = [\"SR-161\", \"LLR-360\"]\n level = \"Unit\"\n-method = \"Exercise each state of the hat block: a non-round neither reads the roster nor asks a perspective question; a first-approved system requirement or amended approved need supplies each applicable parent need; work-item tags widen one need without merging siblings; an absent roster supplies the no-perspective line; an unreadable roster refuses and names it; each applicable perspective receives one non-ruling outcome line; declared template slots receive the block while undeclared slots compose unchanged; a combined sitting carries one union block; and those outcome lines do not alter parsed row rulings or judged rows.\"\n+method = \"Exercise each state of the hat block: a non-round neither reads the roster nor asks a perspective question; a first-approved system requirement or amended approved need makes the round, and every judged system requirement's need and every amended need is a parent; work-item tags widen one need without merging siblings; an absent roster supplies the no-perspective line; an unreadable roster refuses and names it; each applicable perspective receives one non-ruling outcome line; declared template slots receive the block while undeclared slots compose unchanged; a combined sitting carries one union block; and those outcome lines do not alter parsed row rulings or judged rows.\"\n tier = \"Full\"\n expected = \"Satisfies LLR-360 (parent SR-161): a decomposition-round sitting presents each applicable perspective question and requires one outcome, while another sitting has no perspective question; optional-slot, combined-sitting, absent-roster, unreadable-roster, and verdict-parsing outcomes remain as stated.\"\n automated = \"Yes\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
